[h1]Random New World 1.2.2[/h1]

Smoother drawn lands, a unified land editor and lower memory use. For EU5 1.4.7.

[h2]🔧 Fixes and improvements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Cut subcontinents through the land's narrow parts instead of along straight rows. Islands and peninsulas stay together, and South America keeps more of its share when a world has several land arms.
[*]Drawn land now stretches smoothly onto the map. The [b]Land editor…[/b] combines sketches, images, templates and terrain painting; it also includes Westeros, Tamriel, Kalimdor and Ansalon as starting maps.
[*]Generation needs about 8 GB of free RAM instead of 9 GB. The final map check reads in strips, with no change to the reference world's bytes.
[*]Turn on [b]Experimental features[/b] in Settings to choose algorithm epoch 63, 62 (1.2.1) or 61 (1.2.0). It is off by default.
[/list]

[quote][b]Updating:[/b] For EU5 1.4.7. Generate a new world for the new land layout and drawn coasts; keep the original world mod for existing saves. A code from 1.2.1 can make a different world with the default epoch 63. Choose epoch 62 in [b]Experimental features[/b] to make the earlier algorithm again. Use one RNW world at a time and restart EU5 when switching maps.[/quote]

